    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ReWOO and Plan-and-Execute: Decoupled Planning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core toy ReWOO (Planner / Worker / Solver + dependency resolution) lives in `code/main.py` (stdlib-only scripted version). The full interactive Jupyter notebook demo with live LLM calls for the planner and workers is in `code/notebook.py`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The demo answers \"What is the population of the capital of France, rounded to millions?\" using a two-step plan: (1) look up the capital, (2) look up the population, then solve."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Run the notebook (JupyterLite):**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Open `code/notebook.py` in the lesson's JupyterLite environment (or run `python3 -m jupyter notebook code/notebook.py` after setup)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- The notebook steps through the planner, parses the plan, resolves references, executes workers, and composes the solver output."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The trace shows the full plan first, then worker results, then solver composition. Compare the token count (we print a rough character count) to a ReAct-style interleaved run \u2014 ReWOO wins on this kind of structured task."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Parallelize worker execution for independent plan nodes. What does it buy you on a 6-node DAG with 2 parallel groups?\n2. Add a replanner node that fires if any worker returns an error. What is the smallest change to ReWOO that makes it Plan-and-Execute?\n3. Replace `Planner` with a small model (7B class) and keep `Solver` on a frontier model. Compare end-to-end quality \u2014 where does the split fail?\n4. Read Section 4 of the ReWOO paper on planner distillation. Reproduce the 175B -> 7B result conceptually: what training data do you need, and how do you score plan quality?\n5. Port the toy to Plan-and-Act's trajectory shape: plan is a sequence, not a DAG. What tradeoffs change?"
      ]
    }
  ],
